[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Rules
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. Every function that C exports (non-`static`) becomes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    #[unsafe(no_mangle)]
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    pub unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn js_foo(J: *mut js_State, ...) -> ... { unsafe { ... } }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `extern "C-unwind"` (NOT `extern "C"`) — unwinding must cross these boundaries.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `static` C functions become `unsafe fn` or `unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (the latter is required if the function is used as a `js_CFunction` value).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Keep the C names verbatim, including the namespace macros from headers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`utf.h`: chartorune -> `jsU_chartorune`, etc.; `regexp.h`: regcomp ->
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_regcomp`, regexec -> `js_regexec`, regfree -> `js_regfree`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    regcompx -> `js_regcompx`, regfreex -> `js_regfreex`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. Types: `int`->`c_int`, `unsigned`->`c_uint`, `double`->`f64`, `char*`->
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `*mut c_char`, `const char*`->`*const c_char`, `void*`->`*mut c_void`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `short`->`c_short`. Function pointer typedefs (`js_CFunction`, ...) are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `Option<unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn ...>` — pass `Some(f)` / `None`, call with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `(f.unwrap())(J)` or `if let Some(f) = ... { f(J) }`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. Use raw pointers and `(*p).field` everywhere, mirroring the C. Do not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    introduce references/lifetimes/Vec/Box for interpreter data. Allocate with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_malloc`/`js_realloc`/`js_free` from `crate::jsrun` exactly where C does.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. C string literals: use `c"..."` literals and `.as_ptr()`, e.g.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `strcmp(name, c"length".as_ptr())`. libc functions (`strlen`, `strcmp`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `memcpy`, `snprintf`, `printf`, `fmod`, `floor`, `pow`, ...) are declared in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `crate::common`; use them instead of Rust std equivalents so formatting and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    rounding match C exactly. `isnan/isinf/isfinite/signbit` are helper fns in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `common`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. Errors: the variadic C functions become macros already defined at crate root:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_error!(J, c"fmt", args...)`, `js_typeerror!`, `js_rangeerror!`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_syntaxerror!`, `js_referenceerror!`, `js_urierror!`, `js_evalerror!`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    They diverge (`-> !`). Import with e.g. `use crate::{js_typeerror, js_rangeerror};`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    The format string must be a `c"..."` literal; extra args are passed to snprintf.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. `if (js_try(J)) { HANDLER } BODY js_endtry(J);` translates to:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    if js_try(J, || { BODY; js_endtry(J); }).is_err() { HANDLER }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`js_try` is in `common.rs`; note the closure must call `js_endtry` itself,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    exactly like the C success path.) If BODY produces a value used later, return
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    it from the closure and `match` on the `Result`. `js_throw(J)` diverges.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. Enum constants (`JS_TNUMBER`, `JS_CARRAY`, `OP_ADD`, `TK_IF`, `EXP_ADD`, ...)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    are `c_int` consts in `types.rs`. `js_Object.type` is the field `type_`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_Value` is a union: use `.ty()`, `.set_ty(t)`, `.num()`, `.boolean()`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `.litstr()`, `.memstr()`, `.object()`, `.shrstr_ptr()`, `.shrstr_mut()`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `.is_string()`, `.to_str_ptr()` helpers, or `(*v).u.number` etc. directly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_Object.u` is a union too: `(*obj).u.a.length`, `(*obj).u.s.string`, ...
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Flexible array members (`js_Property.name`, `js_Iterator.name`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `js_String.p`) are `[c_char; 1]`; get a pointer with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `(&raw mut (*node).name) as *mut c_char` and size allocations with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `std::mem::offset_of!(js_Property, name)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. `goto` must be restructured with loops/flags/early returns while keeping
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    identical semantics and identical order of side effects.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 9. Integer arithmetic: C wraps. Use `wrapping_*` where overflow is possible, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `as` casts for narrowing. Signed `<<` on ints: cast through `u32`/`u64`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Never let Rust panic (no indexing that can go out of bounds, no `/ 0`,
