[1mVerification[22m — I built the original C library with CMake and compared it against the Rust build using three C drivers (linked against each [38;5;10m.so[0m in turn) plus seven JS test files:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
| check | result |[0m[0m
|---|---|[0m[0m
| exported symbols | 237 in C, 237 in Rust, zero difference |[0m[0m
| language/builtins, JSON, regexp, unicode, GC | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| syntax-error messages incl. file:line | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| number formatting fuzz (400 random doubles × toString/toFixed/toExponential/toPrecision/radix) | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| regexp fuzz (250 patterns × 4 flag sets × 15 subjects, all of test/exec/replace/search/match/split) | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| string-method fuzz (~600 calls + fromCharCode sweep) | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| Date across TZ=UTC/New_York/Tokyo/Berlin | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| C API: userdata w/ has/put/delete/finalize, iterators, accessors, refs/registry, stack ops, [38;5;10mjs_setlimit[0m run+mem limits, panic handler, GC report strings, finalizer order | byte-identical |[0m[0m
| mixed C [38;5;10mjs_try[0m/setjmp frames interleaved with JS try frames | byte-identical |[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mTwo design points worth knowing:[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- *Exceptions.* C MuJS throws via [38;5;10msetjmp[0m/[38;5;10mlongjmp[0m. Calling [38;5;10msetjmp[0m from Rust is unsound, so internal try frames unwind with a Rust panic caught by [38;5;10mcatch_unwind[0m (hence [38;5;10mpanic = "unwind"[0m and [38;5;10mextern "C-unwind"[0m on every exported function and callback type). Frames created through the public [38;5;10mjs_savetry[0m/[38;5;10mjs_savetrypc[0m API are tagged and still use a real [38;5;10mlongjmp[0m, so C callers' [38;5;10mjs_try(J)[0m macro keeps working — verified by driver 3.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- *Bugs found by the differential tests.* Two real defects surfaced and were fixed: [38;5;10mpanic = "abort"[0m in the release profile (killed every JS throw), and my first [38;5;10mOP_TRY[0m implementation, which recursed once per [3mexecution[23m of a try rather than per active try block and blew the native stack in loops. The interpreter now returns a [38;5;10mFlow::EndTry[0m at [38;5;10mOP_ENDTRY[0m, keeping stack depth proportional to active try blocks, matching C.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
C bugs and quirks are reproduced rather than fixed, including MuJS's mangled [38;5;10m'\'[0m token name, the exception value lost when a [38;5;10mcatch[0m with [38;5;10mfinally[0m rethrows, and [38;5;10mjs_strtod[0m's underflow branch that sets a positive exponent.[0m[0m
